### Keep the packaged-app display-name fixture in one place

**Severity:** `low` (non-blocking test maintainability)

Use one local constant for the display name supplied to the fixture and expected in its title assertion. This keeps those two pieces of test setup in sync while retaining the independent AUMID lookup and identity assertions.

The value and behavior are unchanged. This does not request an empty-AUMID fallback, migration of old pins, different reference-identity assertions, or a rename of the existing tests.

```suggestion
        const string displayName = "Localized Snipping Tool";
        var app = TestDataHelper.CreateTestUWPApplication(displayName);
        MockCache.AddUWPApplication(app);
        var provider = new AllAppsCommandProvider(Page);
        await WaitForPageInitializationAsync();

        var result = provider.GetCommandItem(app.UserModelId);

        Assert.IsNotNull(result);
        Assert.AreEqual(displayName, result.Title);
```
